ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE SPECIAL ACT ON THE CONSTRUCTION OF THE DALGUBIT RAILROAD

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Special Act on the Construction of the Dalgubit Railroad and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.

Article 2 (Matters to be included in master plan) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 8(2)9 of the Special Act on the Construction of the Dalgubit Railroad (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following matters:
  1. A topographic map indicating the planned route for the construction of the Dalgubit Railroad;
  2. Matters regarding connecting transportation with other modes of transportation;
  3. The types, required quantity, and procurement plan of railroad rolling stock to be deployed on the planned route of the Dalgubit Railroad;
  4. A general plan for the operation of railroad rolling stock, taking into account demand forecasts for the Dalgubit Railroad.

Article 3 (Designation of implementer of Dalgubit Railroad construction project) (1) If a public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions intends to implement all or part of the Dalgubit Railroad construction project under Article 9(2) of the Act, it shall submit an application for designation as an implementer of the Dalgubit Railroad construction project, in the form prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, along with the following documents and drawings, to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport:
  1. A project plan;
  2. A financing plan;
  3. A topographic map indicating the planned route for the construction of the Dalgubit Railroad.
  (2) Except as provided in paragraph (1), matters necessary for the designation of an implementer of the Dalgubit Railroad construction project shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 4 (Matters to be included in implementation plan) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 10(1) of the Act means the following matters:
  1. A location map of the project implementation area;
  2. The location, lot number, land category, and area of land, articles, or rights to be expropriated or used (hereinafter referred to as "land, etc."); specifications of ownership and rights other than ownership; and the names and addresses of the owners and right holders thereof;
  3. Design documents, including plan views, cross-sectional views, and construction specifications;
  4. The project implementation period;
  5. A financing plan including the following matters and documents proving such plan (applicable only to the implementer of the Dalgubit Railroad construction project under Article 9(2) of the Act):
  a. An annual investment plan;
  b. An annual financing plan;
  c. A plan for the recovery of investment costs, etc. by year;
  6. A plan for the purchase and compensation of land, etc. located within the project implementation area, and measures for the relocation of residents;
  7. Results of consultations with the heads of relevant administrative agencies regarding traffic impact assessments and environmental impact assessments;
  8. Results of a survey on the current status of national heritage;
  9. Measures to mitigate earthquake damage;
  10. If public facilities, etc. are to be installed to replace existing public facilities, etc. under Article 15(1) of the Act on Railroad Construction and Railroad Facilities Management, as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 5(2) of the Act (that railroad Act is hereinafter referred to as the "Railroad Construction Act" and the replacement facilities as "replacement public facilities, etc."), a plan for the relocation and demolition of the existing public facilities, etc. and a plan for the installation of the replacement public facilities, etc.;
  11. If there exist land and facilities that do not vest in the State under the proviso of Article 17(1) of the Railroad Construction Act, as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 5(2) of the Act, a plan for the disposal of such land and facilities;
  12. Where an implementation plan for the Dalgubit Railroad construction project under the former part of Article 10(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "implementation plan") is to be prepared by section or by facility under the latter part of that paragraph, the details thereof;
  13. Where there are matters subject to deliberation by the Railroad Industry Committee under Article 6 of the Framework Act on Railroad Industry Development under Article 9(2) of the Railroad Construction Act, as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 10(2) of the Act, the details of such matters for deliberation;
  14. Where there are deemed authorizations, permissions, etc. under the subparagraphs of Article 11(1) of the Act, the details thereof;
  15. Documents necessary for consultation with relevant authorizing or permitting administrative authorities under Article 24 of the Framework Act on Administration, as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 11(2) of the Act;
  16. Where the project is subject to deliberation by a technical advisory committee under Article 19(5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Construction Technology Promotion Act (limited to deliberation related to design), documents necessary for such deliberation.

Article 5 (Preferential treatment of local enterprises) (1) "Contract for construction works, goods, services, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 14 of the Act means the following:
  1. Contracts for the following works:
  a. General construction works under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Framework Act on the Construction Industry and specialized construction works under subparagraph 6 of that Article;
  b. Electrical works under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Electrical Construction Business Act;
  c. Information and communications works under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Information and Communications Construction Business Act;
  d. Firefighting system installation works under (1)1b of Article 2 of the Firefighting System Installation Business Act;
  2. Contracts for manufacturing and purchasing equipment and materials, machinery, office devices, computer systems, etc. to implement the works under the items of subparagraph 1;
  3. Contracts for services for the following:
  a. Engineering activities under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Engineering Industry Promotion Act;
  b. Design under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Certified Architects Act and construction supervision under subparagraph 4 of that Article.
  (2) If an implementer of the Dalgubit Railroad construction project under Article 9 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "project implementer") intends to grant preferential treatment under Article 14 of the Act, the project implementer shall establish standards for preferential treatment after consultation with the Minister of Finance and Economy and the Minister of Planning and Budget, taking into account the nature of the contract. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2025>
  (3) If a project implementer establishes standards for preferential treatment under paragraph (2), it shall post their details on its website and transmit them to the Integrated Special City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor and Do Governor having jurisdiction over the project area. <Amended on June 23, 2026>
  (4) An Integrated Special City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor or Do Governor having jurisdiction over the project area who receives preferential-treatment standards under paragraph (3) shall post their details on the website of the relevant Integrated Special City, Metropolitan City or Do. <Amended on June 23, 2026>

Article 6 (Public notice of revocation of approval) The public notice under Article 16(2) of the Act shall include the following matters:
  1. The name of the project or the implementation plan;
  2. The name and address of the project implementer (in the case of a corporation, the name and address of the corporation and the name of its representative);
  3. The location and area of the implementation area;
  4. The details of, and reasons for, the disposition or order;
  5. Other matters the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it necessary to publicly notify in connection with a disposition or order.

Article 7 (Criteria for imposition of administrative fines) The criteria for imposing administrative fines under Article 21(1) of the Act shall be as specified in the Appendix.

